From 078e2fad379d32247fe0face9776606d05f11282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:38:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] fix(hermes-vps): make the sending indicator and ready
 marker actually work

The prior sending/ready-marker fix looked correct in offline stub tests
and against direct pane typing, but a live retest against a real
hermes-vps crewmate showed both regressions persisted.

The captain's real steering path is fm-send.sh's durable inbox, delivered
by poll_inbox(), never direct pane typing. poll_inbox() only ran once per
run()'s select() loop iteration, and that loop could block up to
EVENT_WAIT_TIMEOUT (30s) while idle, so a steer could sit unnoticed for
tens of seconds before "[sending...]" ever printed (live-verified: 38s).
INBOX_POLL_INTERVAL is now its own short constant, and run()'s select()
timeout is capped to it whenever --inbox-dir is armed.

The ready marker printed with a trailing newline, leaving the cursor on a
blank line below it instead of beside it. It now prints with no trailing
newline so a real terminal's own input echo continues on the same line;
_forward() supplies the one newline poll_inbox()'s non-echoed path still
needs so "[sending...]" never glues onto the marker's own line.

Both fixes are live-verified against the real VPS (raw pty and tmux).
